.TH SIMRV-CPU-WIZARD 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-cpu-wizard \- create SimRV CPU model configurations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-cpu-wizard
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-cpu-wizard
creates a CPU model configuration interactively or directly from a preset.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Set the configuration name. The default is \fBcustom_riscv\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-template \fIPRESET\fR, \-\-preset \fIPRESET\fR
Choose \fBbalanced\fR, \fBtiny\fR, \fBperformance\fR, or \fBrvcomp\fR.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Write the configuration to this path. By default it is written below
\fBconfigs/models/\fR using the configuration name.
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Generate the configuration without prompting for adjustments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1)
